"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2846,"Narrated to me Ahmad ibn Abi Suraij al-Razi, that 'Amr ibn Mujammi' al-Kindi informed them, on the authority of Musa ibn 'Uqba, on the authority of Nafi', on the authority of Ibn 'Umar (RA), who said:

""When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would mount his riding beast at Dhu al-Hulayfah during a Hajj or 'Umrah, he would say the Talbiyah.""

He then mentioned the hadith and said:

""He stopped at 'Arafah until the sun had set. Then he proceeded, remembering Allah, magnifying Him, declaring His Oneness, and glorifying Him with 'La ilaha illallah' until he reached Muzdalifah.""

**CHAPTER:**"
